## Reflection and Self Assessment

This assignment has improved my understanding in merge sort alogrithm. 
Through this, it has taught me how to divide the sorting work between threads.
I learned how to use pthread_create() to create different threads for sorting different sections and pthread_join() to wait for each section to finishing sorting.
I also learned that increasing the thread count does not always improve performance, as having more threads increases the overhead load which can outweigh the speedup.

A challenge that I faced during the assignment was understanding when to join threads and who should free each argument struct.
During testing, we encountered errors where we had multiple functions freeing up the same argument. We fixed this by commenting out the functions to indentify the error. This help us indentified the caller function that is responsible for freeing the argument.

